### Final Code Review: Watchdog & CLI Argument Validation

**Verdict:** **No blockers for merging the baseline infrastructure.** All previously identified watchdog, diagnostic retention, and CLI parsing blockers are resolved.

---

### 1. Process-Group Watchdog & Diagnostic Retention ([run.py](file:///private/tmp/spawned-baseline-review/benchmarks/run.py), [test_runner.py](file:///private/tmp/spawned-baseline-review/benchmarks/test_runner.py))
- **Session & Process-Group Teardown:** [`run_sample`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-baseline-review/benchmarks/run.py#L36-L54) launches `/usr/bin/time` and the benchmark binary in a dedicated session (`start_new_session=True`) with `LC_ALL='C'`. On `TimeoutExpired` or any other `BaseException` (including interrupts), `os.killpg(process.pid, signal.SIGKILL)` terminates both `/usr/bin/time` and the spawned benchmark descendant processes while ignoring `ProcessLookupError` if already exited.
- **Diagnostic Preservation:** After signaling the process group, [`run_sample`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-baseline-review/benchmarks/run.py#L48-L51) drains `process.communicate()` and writes both `<stem>.stdout` and `<stem>.stderr` before re-raising, ensuring timeout/crash output is never lost.
- **Resource & Output Validation:** [`main`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-baseline-review/benchmarks/run.py#L65-L147) verifies `/usr/bin/time` exists upfront, validates single-row well-formed CSV stdout, requires parsed `process_peak_rss_bytes` and `process_cpu_s` to be non-empty, gates summary allocation statistics on `allocation_counting == 'true'`, and builds `summary.csv` headers across all summary rows (`dict.fromkeys`) so mixed allocation-enabled/disabled runs serialize cleanly.
- **Real Subprocess Regression Test:** [`WatchdogTests.test_timeout_kills_grandchild_and_preserves_diagnostics`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-baseline-review/benchmarks/test_runner.py#L13-L31) spawns a real child and grandchild process, triggers a 1s timeout, verifies `.stdout`/`.stderr` logs are flushed to disk, and confirms the grandchild PID is terminated.

### 2. CLI Control & Boolean Flag Validation ([args.rs](file:///private/tmp/spawned-baseline-review/concurrency/benches/support/args.rs), [baseline.rs](file:///private/tmp/spawned-baseline-review/concurrency/benches/baseline.rs))
- **Strict Flag Hygiene:** [`validate`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-baseline-review/concurrency/benches/support/args.rs#L2-L15) runs in [`Config::parse`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-baseline-review/concurrency/benches/baseline.rs#L174-L230) before runtime or thread creation. It permits Cargo's `--bench` marker, requires `--key=value` syntax, rejects unknown keys against the explicit allowlist, rejects empty values, and rejects duplicate arguments.
- **Explicit Boolean & Backend Parsing:** `flag` accepts only `"on" | "true"` and `"off" | "false"`, panicking on malformed values instead of silently defaulting to `false`. `config.backend` is also asserted against the five valid backends prior to runtime initialization.
